Pull Request ≠ git pull — Pull Request is a GitHub feature to request merging your branch into main. Pipeline triggers on PR creation and runs tests automatically 
to catch bugs before merging! ✅

Pull Request = request to merge
               branch into main ✅
               GitHub feature ✅

pull_request trigger:
  pipeline runs when
  PR is created ✅
  tests code automatically ✅
  catches bugs before merge ✅
  protects main branch ✅

No! Developer must manually create Pull Request:

Flow — Step by Step

Step 1: Create branch
  git checkout -b feature/login ✅

Step 2: Make changes
  edit code ✅

Step 3: Push branch
  git push origin feature/login ✅
        ↓
  code is on GitHub ✅
  BUT no PR yet ❌

Step 4: Manually create PR
  go to GitHub.com ✅
  click "Compare & pull request" ✅
  OR click "New pull request" ✅
        ↓
  PR created ✅
        ↓
  pipeline triggers ✅


How to Create PR on GitHub

Option 1: GitHub Console
  GitHub.com
  → your repo
  → Pull requests tab
  → New pull request
  → base: main
  → compare: feature/login
  → Create pull request ✅

Compare changes page:
  compares two branches ✅
  shows what changed ✅
  allows creating PR ✅

How to Create PR Correctly

Step 1:
  base    : main          ← keep this
  compare : feature/login ← change this ✅

Step 2:
  GitHub shows differences ✅
  what files changed
  what lines changed

Step 3:
  Click Create pull request ✅

Step 4:
  Add title and description
  Click Create pull request ✅

PR(pull request) created

When Do Tests Run?

AFTER PR created:
        ↓
GitHub Actions triggers ✅
  (because of pull_request trigger)
        ↓
Pipeline runs:
  ✅ build
  ✅ tests
  ✅ code quality
        ↓
PR shows:
  ✅ All checks passed
  ❌ Some checks failed

Tests run:
  ✅ AFTER PR is created
  ✅ GitHub Actions handles
  ✅ automatically ✅

